WEBVTT

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:11.150
The Seven Pillars play an integral role in the tuning ceremony for youkai,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:17.910
but actually, they're just a Trojan horse Hiizumi Enyou came up with, huh?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:50.530
Thanks to you, my adorable toy came all the way here.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.530
So...

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.490
I came to get her back.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.490
You damn thief.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.240
<i>In the night sky beyond this curtain,</i>

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.950
<i>countless stars dot the sky.</i>

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.040
<i>The starry sky that enchants all who see it...</i>

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:13.750
<i>It looks...</i>

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:25.470
Rin

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.460
Morning already?

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.840
The weather's great as usual.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:09.390
Hm? Did I sleep— I mean, die in a weird position?

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.860
Rin-chan, are you awake—

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.780
Sorry for the wait. I'll hurry up.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.710
I'm ready for work, Boss.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.880
O-Okay.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.050
Good morning.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.550
Oh, morning.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.180
Breakfast is ready.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.350
Okay.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.640
Oh, that reminds me...

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.400
Just a little longer.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.400
Thanks for the meal!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.240
I'll take care of the dishes, so you handle the usual delivery, okay?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.160
Okay!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:08.950
Rin.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.050
Lookin' like a real pro now.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.340
Honestly, you know how dangerous that is...

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.390
Oh, she wouldn't get hurt from <i>that</i>.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.010
I'm off then.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:29.800
Yeah!

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:31.850
Take care.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.110
It's been two years since Rin came here, huh?

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.980
She's a nice, hard worker.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.690
A great daughter.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.070
She sure is.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:51.080
But I wonder if we're doing a good job
playing the role of her parents.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.000
<i>It's already been two years since I came to Sakura Newtown.</i>

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:01.090
<i>The boss and her husband take good care of me,</i>

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:01.670
Town Tournament
<b>Innovate! Sakura Newtown Go Association</b>

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:03.590
<i>and the people here are all very kind.
Town Tournament
<b>Innovate! Sakura Newtown Go Association</b></i>

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.300
<i>and the people here are all very kind.</i>

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:12.180
<i>When I first came, there were
countless things I was afraid of</i>

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.100
<i>and nothing I could feel happy about,
so I couldn't even imagine what real joy was like.</i>

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.100
<b>Houhouran
<i>and nothing I could feel happy about,
so I couldn't even imagine what real joy was like.</i></b>

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.100
<b>1 Per
With Seaweed</b>
<b>Large and Freshly Roasted</b>

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:20.900
Houhouran

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:27.990
<i>But this place is filled with open-hearted humans who'd accept even a youkai like me.
Houhouran</i>

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:46.050
<i>I even started attending school and made many, many friends.</i>

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.180
<i>My life's pretty great now.</i>

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.600
Hey, Rinnoji!

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:04.520
Yo.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.900
On a delivery?

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.660
Yep. And you?

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.030
Me?

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.160
I'm... out for this.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:21.170
Around this time every month, I go to Juri-san for a check-up.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.170
A check-up?

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:29.420
I wonder if I should have her take a look at me too.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.260
Oh, no, it's nothing.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:34.300
Ah, that's right.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.930
Akina-san, want some senbei?

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.720
Where'd that come from?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:43.400
I bought a bag at a senbei stand and he gave me another one for free.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.270
I see. Thanks.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.030
Okay, time to go then.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.610
See you around, Rinnoji.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:00.960
A check-up, huh?

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.130
I should let Touka-chan know.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:06.130
Let's Protect Our Beloved Town

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.630
Akina-san's getting a check-up?

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.640
Rin-chan, nice job!

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.060
A chance to be alone together!

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.640
I can't pass it up!

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.140
Hello!

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:23.890
Akina-san...

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.400
and Hime-chan...

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:29.690
Touka.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.280
Oh, Touka-chin.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.450
and Juri-san.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.160
So you're all here.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:40.660
<i>Well, I should've figured Juri-san would be here.</i>

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:46.670
Okay, you seem fine now.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:50.670
But I'd say you need to learn how to manage your strength better.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.170
I'm pretty confident when it comes to my strength, though.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:56.680
I-If we're talking about strength, I'm stronger!

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:00.100
That's not exactly what I mean.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.430
Okay!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.100
Come on.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.360
Let ol' Juri here show you a thing or two.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:10.860
Step right up.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.610
Okay, here we go.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:16.360
Ready, go!

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.370
Huh?

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.370
How come it's not budging?

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:34.970
See?

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:40.640
The important part is how you move your bones and contract your muscles.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.060
If you master that, you lessen the tension and lower the risk of injury.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:49.480
That way, even an ordinary human like me can overpower youkai.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.150
So don't just depend on your innate gifts.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.650
Okay.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.910
Well then, next up is...

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.410
You've deviated quite a bit.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:07.160
Have you been tuning a lot or something?

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:09.920
W-Well...

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:13.670
Here I go then.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:37.820
And that does it.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.200
If you start to feel off again, come see me, okay?

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.290
That's amazing, Juri-san.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.660
I'm not doing anything special.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:50.210
For a tuner to be normalized,

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:54.460
they need to hold hands with a human, a being of this world.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.720
That's how the deviations get neutralized.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.220
So that means...

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.680
even a dog would do?

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:04.720
I don't know about that.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.480
That means that even if a youkai like me...

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:14.730
...or me... holds hands with him...

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:17.740
I don't think it'd help.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.610
I see.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.490
Akina-chin.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:26.450
Yes?

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.950
That reminds me, Yae asked me to pass a message.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:29.460
Whoa, wait...
That reminds me, Yae asked me to pass a message.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:33.380
Wait, Juri-san, what... What is it, Juri-san?!
The Seven Pillars' shrine is broken, so go check it out.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.000
Wait, Juri-san, what... What is it, Juri-san?!

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.310
Do you two like Akina-kun?

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:48.520
I-I'm...

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.850
It's not like being youkai means you can't do anything.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:56.520
Like I said earlier, if you learn how to use your strength properly,

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:00.400
Akina-chin won't have to tune as much.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:07.530
There are things only youkai can do, too.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.040
Hello!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.540
Oh, welcome.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:16.920
Greetings from the Hiizumi Counseling Office.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.800
We've come to pick up what we asked for.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.510
This is for Tanaka-san in the third block,

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.800
this is for Yokoyama-san in the second block,

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.260
and this is for Narimatsu-san in the fourth block.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.310
Thank you very much.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.560
Deliver them safely.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.440
Oh?

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:37.650
Yae-san, where's Takagi-san's from the fourth—

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.990
Hey, you two.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:52.620
Sorry about my perverted brother.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:56.130
It's okay. We're used to it now.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.340
Maybe we should hold a vote of no-confidence against him.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.050
I'd back that.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:06.800
Wh-What's wrong?

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:18.650
Um...

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:21.860
That scarf... Hime-san?

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.400
Oh, hey there.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.030
What's with the bear head?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.950
I borrowed it for the festival,

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:32.080
but when I went to return it earlier
they said it was old and that I could have it.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:36.330
What are you going to use it for?

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.550
Yae-san?

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:50.890
D-Don't you think you're a bit too old
to be playing with teddy bears?

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.940
<b>Always Knock!</b>
Yae-san's... room.

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.110
Hey, what's it like?

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.730
Let's look and see!

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:13.540
Well now, this is really something.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.210
So many teddy bears!

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:19.040
Wow, it's so cute!

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.710
Yeah, it's wonderful!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:22.960
So cute!

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:28.970
You two!

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.520
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.270
Um, Yae-san...

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:36.980
Hm?

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:39.100
Want this?

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.990
So you're on patrol, Hime?

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:49.740
Yeah, it's my turn today.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.620
As diligent as ever.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:57.000
The crime rate's pretty low in this town, isn't it?

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:01.000
Both the number of crimes and arrests are among the lowest.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.540
We're one of the safest towns in the whole Kanto region.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:08.340
Maybe your constant patrolling is really paying off.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.510
It definitely is!

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:15.810
Oh yeah. Speaking of public safety...

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:20.480
There's a gang of thieves causing trouble in the city recently.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.940
They even hit the neighboring town a while ago.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:27.360
That's not something we can ignore. We should redouble the patrols.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.540
Don't worry about that.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:43.000
You need to take this more seriously, Yae-san.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.460
It's gonna be fine.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:49.300
Crime doesn't appear in this town that easily.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.890
That's just how it works.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.530
It's so hot out here.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:16.070
I actually like it.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:16.780
Hey, girls!

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.080
You've got some time tomorrow, right?

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:24.080
There's something I wanna talk to you about. Bring Akina too.

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:26.920
Sure...

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:33.630
See you then.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:52.320
Hold hands, huh?

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.070
Touka!

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:56.280
What are you doing?

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.570
Some kind of magic?

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.330
Kotoha?

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:03.540
Hey! Let's play together!

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:10.250
I heard that Akina drifts a bit further away from this world every time he tunes.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:14.170
It can be fixed by holding hands.

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:17.760
But it doesn't work with youkai?

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:27.650
I might be very strong, but there's stuff youkai can't do.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:33.860
I don't care what the reason is.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.180
I wanna hold hands with Akina-san.

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.700
You know, I'm a half-youkai,

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:52.130
so I can only give half a help to both youkai and humans.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:58.640
But I think there are things only half-youkai can do.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:01.390
I'm sure there are.

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:11.650
So I'm sure there's something only you can do too, Touka.

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:16.490
Oh well.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:20.120
Hey, Ao!

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.160
I'm leaving!

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.660
Laters!

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:27.830
Wanna come?

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:34.920
Hime and the others have got to be hungry. They'll have dinner for you too.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.430
Sure!

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:02.740
The land gods do not exist because there is a town.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:05.370
The town exists because there are land gods.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:10.460
Indeed, this town is me.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:16.590
It seems we've got some vermin crawling about tonight.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:22.840
I shall begin my night patrol.

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:02.260
Let's just do this already, man.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.300
Yeah.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:05.850
See a shop that looks like it'd be loaded?

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:23.820
Who the hell are you?
What are you doing out so late?

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.870
This ain't no forest, little bear.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:29.870
Oh my... You don't say?

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.370
Just fuck off, will ya?!

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:42.800
That was close.

00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:52.980
Don't worry,

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:55.980
I used the hilt.

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:10.330
You surprised me, bitch!

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.080
Pull yourselves together.

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:17.250
Tie that teddy bear bitch up until we're done.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.840
Damn, I'm feeling so dizzy.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.840
Don't you pull any more weird shit.

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:29.010
Hey, quit movin'!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:36.690
Y-You bitch!

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:05.970
Missed by a hair.

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:09.930
G-Gods, help me!

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:12.930
Gods, huh?

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:17.400
Yeah, don't worry. You're right in praying to the gods.

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:23.400
They're watching, after all.

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:32.990
How pathetic.

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:34.700
Geez.

00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:58.020
Please take care of this!

00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:01.270
I guess I can handle this.

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:10.780
Did you lose your cool?

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:13.780
Who knows?

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:18.290
I hear some thieves showed up yesterday.

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:24.540
They claimed that a teddy bear caught them.

00:23:24.540 --> 00:23:28.970
They must've smoked something weird.

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:34.550
The shrine at the Pillar was
destroyed in a very unusual way.

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:38.050
It looked worn down...

00:23:38.970 --> 00:23:41.560
as if it rotted away.

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:49.570
Well, I wanted to warn you about something regarding that.

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:51.150
Ah, brother.

00:23:51.150 --> 00:23:52.320
When did you get here?

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:54.660
Come on!

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:55.620
Never mind him.

00:23:57.540 --> 00:24:01.000
There's a good reason why I've asked all of you here today.

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:08.000
Enjin's made his move.

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:12.510
Cleaning

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:15.510
That's right, my body is...

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:20.520
I must deliver...

00:24:23.730 --> 00:24:24.770
Zakuro's property

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:35.200
His goal is to make the Seven Pillars bloom.

00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:37.910
His grudge goes back a ways in history.

00:24:37.910 --> 00:24:40.040
Don't underestimate his hatred.

00:24:43.160 --> 00:24:47.290
The problem is that he used to act alone,

00:24:47.290 --> 00:24:51.420
but now he's teamed up with a troublesome bunch.

00:24:56.090 --> 00:24:58.300
Youkai Hunters?

00:24:59.060 --> 00:25:02.810
Under certain conditions,
they wield immense powers.

00:25:03.390 --> 00:25:05.810
You could call them the natural enemies of youkai.

00:25:06.440 --> 00:25:08.820
And there's not just one or two of them.

00:25:09.690 --> 00:25:12.240
The threat they each pose is off the charts.

00:25:19.200 --> 00:25:22.330
As you are now, you stand no chance whatsoever.

00:25:25.170 --> 00:25:26.420
A dragon killer.

00:25:29.670 --> 00:25:31.130
A vampire hunter.

00:25:33.300 --> 00:25:34.470
An exorcist.

00:25:36.340 --> 00:25:37.340
And...

00:25:45.730 --> 00:25:47.190
A necromancer.

00:25:54.070 --> 00:25:54.940
Rin-chan!

00:26:03.950 --> 00:26:05.080
Brother?

00:26:05.750 --> 00:26:06.460
Are you okay?

00:26:08.460 --> 00:26:09.420
Rin-chan?

00:26:23.970 --> 00:26:24.720
Rin?

00:26:50.330 --> 00:26:55.420
Where did all that strength come from?

00:26:57.220 --> 00:26:59.430
